From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason920612 <jasonya2206@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:07:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Tile-parallel ticking of entities, block entities and chunk
 random ticks (-Dquire.parallel=true)

Units are grouped into tiles coloured 3x3; same-coloured tiles tick concurrently on TileWorker threads, each confined to its tile plus one ring. Out-of-area access, plugin event dispatch and global side effects (explosions, teleports, redstone wire/torches, stats, advancements, scoreboard, POI changes, tree/mushroom growth capture) escalate the worker to exclusive execution; plugin listeners and chunk loads run on the real main thread. Global entity callbacks are deferred and replayed on the main thread in task order. Shared generators, neighbour updaters and path type caches are per worker. Off by default.

